From: OHOS adaptation <build@ohpcd>
Subject: [PATCH] Guard outStream references in ModemFSK/ModemGMSK under ENABLE_DIGITAL_LAB

Upstream CubicSDR 0.2.7 references the ModemDigital::outStream member in
ModemFSK.cpp and ModemGMSK.cpp unconditionally, but the member is only
declared when ENABLE_DIGITAL_LAB is set (ModemDigital.h, `#if
ENABLE_DIGITAL_LAB`).  Building with ENABLE_DIGITAL_LAB=0 -- the upstream
CMakeLists.txt default -- therefore fails to compile these two files:

  src/modules/modem/digital/ModemFSK.cpp:12:5: error: use of undeclared identifier 'outStream'
  src/modules/modem/digital/ModemGMSK.cpp:11:5: error: use of undeclared identifier 'outStream'

(The upstream travis-ci configuration builds with -DENABLE_DIGITAL_LAB=1,
which masks this defect.)

The HarmonyOS PC core-library cut compiles with ENABLE_DIGITAL_LAB=0:

  1. the Digital Lab console GUI that consumes the outStream bytes is a
     wxWidgets window (src/forms/DigitalConsole) -- out of scope on a
     platform without wxCore GUI, so the stream has no consumer;
  2. the std::stringstream member instantiated inside the static library
     triggers an OHOS toolchain weak-symbol duplication issue at process
     exit (inline-namespace weak copy in the .a vs the libc++_shared.so
     copy -> invalid free in ios_base::~ios_base at static destruction;
     verified with AddressSanitizer on a minimal digital-modem
     construct/destroy probe: analog modems exit cleanly, digital modems
     crash 100% reproducibly).

Guarding the two references keeps upstream behaviour identical for every
configuration that compiles today (LAB=1 still streams; LAB=0 previously
did not build these translation units at all) while making the LAB=0
core cut compile and run cleanly.  The demodulator state-machine calls
(fskdem_demodulate / gmskdem_demodulate) are preserved on the LAB=0 path
so symbol timing and buffer progression stay upstream-identical.

---
diff --git a/src/modules/modem/digital/ModemFSK.cpp b/src/modules/modem/digital/ModemFSK.cpp
index 7bec57d..9503752 100644
--- a/src/modules/modem/digital/ModemFSK.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/modem/digital/ModemFSK.cpp
@@ -9,7 +9,9 @@ ModemFSK::ModemFSK() : ModemDigital()  {
     bps = 1;
     sps = 9600;
     bw = 0.45f;
+#if ENABLE_DIGITAL_LAB
     outStream << std::hex;
+#endif
 }
 
 ModemBase *ModemFSK::factory() {
@@ -134,7 +136,11 @@ void ModemFSK::demodulate(ModemKit *kit, ModemIQData *input, AudioThreadInput *
     dkit->inputBuffer.insert(dkit->inputBuffer.end(),input->data.begin(),input->data.end());
 
     while (dkit->inputBuffer.size() >= dkit->k) {
+#if ENABLE_DIGITAL_LAB
         outStream << fskdem_demodulate(dkit->demodFSK, &dkit->inputBuffer[0]);
+#else
+        (void)fskdem_demodulate(dkit->demodFSK, &dkit->inputBuffer[0]);
+#endif
         
 //        float err = fskdem_get_frequency_error(dkit->demodFSK);
         dkit->inputBuffer.erase(dkit->inputBuffer.begin(),dkit->inputBuffer.begin()+dkit->k);
diff --git a/src/modules/modem/digital/ModemGMSK.cpp b/src/modules/modem/digital/ModemGMSK.cpp
index 3aaff85..8e75a85 100644
--- a/src/modules/modem/digital/ModemGMSK.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/modem/digital/ModemGMSK.cpp
@@ -8,7 +8,9 @@ ModemGMSK::ModemGMSK() : ModemDigital()  {
     _sps = 4;
     _fdelay = 3;
     _ebf = 0.3f;
+#if ENABLE_DIGITAL_LAB
     outStream << std::hex;
+#endif
 }
 
 ModemGMSK::~ModemGMSK() = default;
@@ -124,7 +126,11 @@ void ModemGMSK::demodulate(ModemKit *kit, ModemIQData *input, AudioThreadInput *
     int numProcessed = 0;
     for (size_t i = 0, iMax = dkit->inputBuffer.size()/dkit->sps; i < iMax; i+= dkit->sps) {
         gmskdem_demodulate(dkit->demodGMSK, &input->data[i],&sym_out);
+#if ENABLE_DIGITAL_LAB
         outStream << sym_out;
+#else
+        (void)sym_out;
+#endif
         numProcessed += dkit->sps;
     }
     
